  "scenarioKind": "partial_validity_correction",
  "title": "Partial-validity correction: a correction scoped to one interval must not erase the other intervals",
  "provenance": {
    "specRefs": ["tasks/spec-v0.2/data-execution.md#D3", "tasks/prd-industry-semantic-agent-v0.2.md#US-017"],
    "functionalRequirements": ["FR-19", "FR-20"],
    "userStories": ["US-017"],
    "acceptanceRefs": ["US-017.A2"],
    "derivation": "D3.1: a correction/retraction is a new event scoped to an explicit validity interval and never overwrites the historical payload; a partial-interval correction does not erase the other intervals and projections may split. The correction covers only [12:00,18:00), so validAt before 12:00 and at/after 18:00 still resolve the original value, and the pre-correction recorded version never shows the correction."
  },
